#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Notes"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "`TRADITIONAL`"
msgstr "`TRADITIONAL`"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid ""
"Conjunction, Semi-sextile, Sextile, Square, Trine, Quincunx, Opposition "
"(7 aspects)"
msgstr ""
"Conjonction, Semi-sextile, Sextile, Carré, Trigone, Quinconce, Opposition"
" (7 aspects)"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "**Library default** (v1.3+)"
msgstr "**Défaut de la bibliothèque** (v1.3+)"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "`CLASSICAL`"
msgstr "`CLASSICAL`"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "Conjunction, Sextile, Square, Trine, Opposition (5 aspects)"
msgstr "Conjonction, Sextile, Carré, Trigone, Opposition (5 aspects)"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "v1.2 and earlier default"
msgstr "Défaut de v1.2 et antérieures"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "`EXTENDED`"
msgstr "`EXTENDED`"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "All 14 aspects"
msgstr "Les 14 aspects"

#: ../../source/api.md
msgid "Includes full-circle minors (H5/H9/H10)"
msgstr "Inclut les mineurs plein-cercle (H5/H9/H10)"

#: ../../source/api.md:185
msgid "All presets are `numpy.ndarray` boolean masks over the 14-aspect table."
msgstr ""
"Tous les prédéfinis sont des masques booléens `numpy.ndarray` sur la "
"table des 14 aspects."

#: ../../source/api.md:187
msgid ""
"`AspectSetSpec = Union[str, list, numpy.ndarray, None]` — any of these "
"can be passed as the `aspects` argument to `calculate_aspects`."
msgstr ""
"`AspectSetSpec = Union[str, list, numpy.ndarray, None]` — l'un quelconque"
" de ces types peut être passé comme argument `aspects` à "
"`calculate_aspects`."

#: ../../source/api.md:189
msgid "`aspects_for_harmonics(harmonics)`"
msgstr "`aspects_for_harmonics(harmonics)`"

#: ../../source/api.md:191
msgid ""
"Compose a custom aspect set from a list of harmonics. Returns a frozen "
"length-14 `numpy.bool_` mask that can be used as `aspects=` argument to "
"any Ketu function."
msgstr ""
"Compose un ensemble d'aspects personnalisé à partir d'une liste "
"d'harmoniques. Retourne un masque `numpy.bool_` gelé de longueur 14 "
"utilisable comme argument `aspects=` dans toute fonction Ketu."

#: ../../source/api.md:195
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`harmonics` (`Sequence[int]`): list of harmonic integers; valid values: "
"`{1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 9, 10}`"
msgstr ""
"`harmonics` (`Sequence[int]`) : liste d'entiers harmoniques ; valeurs "
"valides : `{1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 9, 10}`"

#: ../../source/api.md:197
msgid "**Returns:** frozen `numpy.ndarray` of `numpy.bool_`, shape `(14,)`"
msgstr "**Retourne :** `numpy.ndarray` gelé de `numpy.bool_`, forme `(14,)`"

#: ../../source/api.md:199
msgid ""
"**Raises:** `ValueError` if any harmonic is not in the valid set or is "
"not an integer."
msgstr ""
"**Lève :** `ValueError` si un harmonique n'est pas dans l'ensemble valide"
" ou n'est pas un entier."

#: ../../source/api.md:221
msgid "`generate_harmonic_aspects(h)`"
msgstr "`generate_harmonic_aspects(h)`"

#: ../../source/api.md:223
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Generate aspect specs on the fly for **any** integer harmonic `h` — not "
"just the named preset harmonics `{1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 9, 10}`. For each `k = 1"
" … h//2`, the function computes `angle = fold_to_0_180(k · 360 / h)` and "
"`coef = k / h`, using the full-circle 360° convention folded to 0–180°."
msgstr ""
"Génère des spécifications d'aspects à la volée pour **tout** harmonique "
"entier `h` — pas uniquement les harmoniques des presets nommés "
"`{1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 9, 10}`. Pour chaque `k = 1 … h//2`, la fonction "
"calcule `angle = fold_to_0_180(k · 360 / h)` et `coef = k / h`, en "
"utilisant la convention plein-cercle 360° repliée sur 0–180°."

#: ../../source/api.md:227
msgid ""
"`h` (`int`): the harmonic, `2 ≤ h ≤ 64`. `h = 1` is rejected (degenerate,"
" 0 rows); `h > 64` is rejected (impractically small orbs)."
msgstr ""
"`h` (`int`) : l'harmonique, `2 ≤ h ≤ 64`. `h = 1` est rejeté "
"(dégénéré, 0 lignes) ; `h > 64` est rejeté (orbes impraticablement "
"petits)."

#: ../../source/api.md:229
msgid ""
"**Returns:** structured array with the **same dtype as `core.aspects`** "
"(drop-in), shape `(h // 2,)`. Names are auto-generated (`b'H7-1'`, "
"`b'H7-2'`, …). Pass the result as the `dynamic_specs=` argument to "
"`calculate_aspects`, `find_aspects_between_dates`, and "
"`calculate_synastry`."
msgstr ""
"**Retourne :** tableau structuré avec le **même dtype que `core.aspects`**"
" (substitut direct), forme `(h // 2,)`. Les noms sont auto-générés "
"(`b'H7-1'`, `b'H7-2'`, …). Passe le résultat comme argument "
"`dynamic_specs=` à `calculate_aspects`, `find_aspects_between_dates` et "
"`calculate_synastry`."

#: ../../source/api.md:231
msgid "**Raises:** `ValueError` if `h` is not an `int` or is outside `[2, 64]`."
msgstr ""
"**Lève :** `ValueError` si `h` n'est pas un `int` ou est en dehors de "
"`[2, 64]`."

#: ../../source/api.md:248
msgid ""
"**Note on orbs:** Dynamic harmonic orbs use `coef = k / h` (full-circle "
"convention). For high harmonics this yields orbs roughly half the size of"
" the equivalent half-circle aspect — accepted behaviour; the two "
"conventions coexist without unification (see the v1.4 release notes)."
msgstr ""
"**Note sur les orbes :** Les orbes des harmoniques dynamiques utilisent "
"`coef = k / h` (convention plein-cercle). Pour les harmoniques élevés, "
"cela donne des orbes environ deux fois plus petits que l'aspect demi-cercle"
" équivalent — comportement accepté ; les deux conventions coexistent sans "
"unification (voir les notes de version v1.4)."

#: ../../source/api.md:250
msgid "`core.aspects` columns: `harmonic` and `symbol`"
msgstr "`core.aspects` columns: `harmonic` and `symbol`"

#: ../../source/api.md:252
msgid ""
"`core.aspects` is a 5-field structured array `(name, angle, coef, "
"harmonic, symbol)`. New in v1.3: the `harmonic` and `symbol` columns."
msgstr ""
"`core.aspects` est un tableau structuré à 5 champs `(name, angle, coef, "
"harmonic, symbol)`. Nouveau en v1.3 : les colonnes `harmonic` et "
"`symbol`."

#: ../../source/api.md:255
msgid ""
"**`harmonic` (`int32`):** the harmonic base for each aspect. Values: `[1,"
" 6, 10, 9, 3, 5, 9, 2, 10, 3, 5, 6, 9, 1]` for aspects 0–13 in the "
"canonical table order. `aspects_for_harmonics` uses this column "
"internally (data-driven, no hardcoded indices)."
msgstr ""
"**`harmonic` (`int32`) :** la base harmonique de chaque aspect. Valeurs :"
" `[1, 6, 10, 9, 3, 5, 9, 2, 10, 3, 5, 6, 9, 1]` pour les aspects 0–13 "
"dans l'ordre canonique de la table. `aspects_for_harmonics` utilise cette"
" colonne en interne (piloté par les données, sans indices codés en dur)."

#: ../../source/api.md:256
msgid ""
"**`symbol` (`U4`):** Unicode glyph for the 7 half-circle aspects (☌ ⚺ ⚹ □"
" △ ⚻ ☍); blank (`\"\"`) for the 7 full-circle minor aspects."
msgstr ""
"**`symbol` (`U4`) :** glyphe Unicode pour les 7 aspects demi-cercle (☌ ⚺ "
"⚹ □ △ ⚻ ☍) ; vide (`\"\"`) pour les 7 aspects mineurs plein-cercle."

#: ../../source/api.md:257
msgid ""
"**`coef` (`float32`):** orb coefficient. Conceptually referred to as "
"`coefficient` in API documentation; the field name in the dtype is `coef`"
" and was **not renamed** in v1.3."
msgstr ""
"**`coef` (`float32`) :** coefficient d'orbe. Conceptuellement désigné "
"comme `coefficient` dans la documentation API ; le nom du champ dans le "
"dtype est `coef` et n'a **pas été renommé** en v1.3."

#: ../../source/api.md:268
msgid "`get_aspect(jday, body1, body2)`"
msgstr "`get_aspect(jday, body1, body2)`"

#: ../../source/api.md:270
msgid ""
"Return the aspect between two bodies, or `None` if no in-orb aspect "
"exists."
msgstr ""
"Retourne l'aspect entre deux corps, ou `None` si aucun aspect dans l'orbe"
" n'existe."

#: ../../source/api.md:272
msgid ""
"**Returns:** `tuple[int, int, int, float]` → `(body1, body2, aspect_id, "
